      "Yorke knows this the way other people know their own pulse. She measured it at first light with the sextant and a stopwatch and the marker posts Kael welded to the eastern pontoons, and the number is twelve point one, down from twelve point four at the turn of the year, and the arithmetic of that decline is a thing she does not say out loud in council meetings because Reika has asked her not to frighten people with numbers they cannot use.",
      "She can use the numbers. That's the difference. She is the only one who can use the numbers.",
      "The deep nets come up heavy for the first time in eleven weeks. Taryn's vertical rigging worked: nets down forty metres on anchored cables, lifted by the crane they built out of trawler winches, and today they come up silver and thrashing, forty kilos, sixty, ninety — Nikos is shouting numbers from the deck of the *Ayia Marina* and Emiko Voss is laughing in a way that carries.",
      "One hundred and ten kilos. More than double the ration target. Enough to salt, enough to trade, enough to feed everyone for four days with leftovers.",
      "The whole eastern cluster comes out to watch the crane. Somebody bangs a wrench on a pot. Yuki Voss, fourteen, sits on a crate with her sketchbook and doesn't draw, just watches, which for Yuki is the highest compliment available.",
      "Dr. Seo-yun Park takes samples from the catch and logs them and spends the afternoon unhappy.",
      "\"What,\" Yorke says, at the evening council in Reika's lifeboat, tea in the mismatched cups.",
      "\"The catch wasn't one species. It was eleven species that don't school together.\" Seo-yun lays the tally on the table. \"They were running. Something pushed them up from below.\"",
      "\"Something like what?\"",
      "\"Cold water. A mass of it, coming up from the deep, deeper than the light reaches.\" Seo-yun taps her own chart, the one nobody wants to read. \"Or the top layer is thinning and the deep layer is rising to replace it. Which would mean the patch isn't just shrinking at the edges. It's shallowing.\"",
      "Reika pours more tea. That is Reika's answer to everything, and it has worked for nine years.",
      "\"So we caught a good day,\" Taryn says.",
      "\"So we caught a symptom,\" Seo-yun says.",
      "Yorke drinks her tea and does not say that she has known this for four months. She has known it since the panels started reading three percent low in the same week the water temperature dropped half a degree, and she hasn't said it because a thing said in a council meeting becomes a thing that has to be answered, and she doesn't have an answer.",
      "Tonight the plankton come up. This is the third night running. The water under the boats goes luminous and blue, drifting in long ropes of light that coil and uncoil with the swell, and people come out on the platforms and stand at the railings and look at it because it is beautiful and because there is nothing else to look at that isn't water or rope or another platform.",
      "Kael's crews have finished the first new structure off the salvaged eastern pontoons: a raised deck, six by four metres, on four lashed aluminium columns. Tomorrow they build the second. In six weeks they'll have a schoolhouse up there, off the damp, and the children will learn their letters eleven metres above the fish.",
