      "But she will be. She knows she will be. She wrote the number on her hand so she could not forget, and now she cannot forget, and the number is still there, eleven point five, and the tide is still moving, and the council is still talking about the schoolhouse, and she sits in the curve of Reika's lifeboat and listens to them talk about the schoolhouse because that is what people do when they do not know what else to do."
