      "He is pointing east, out past the bow, out past the grey, into the dark.",
      "There is a light.",
      "Not the sun. The sun is behind them, west, where it always is. This is a point of light in the dark, low on the horizon, steady, not a star because there are no stars through the haze, not a boat because no boat would be out there in the dark alone.",
      "\"How long has it been there?\" Yorke asks.",
      "\"Since the welding stopped,\" Nikos says. \"I thought it was a reflection. Reflections move. That does not move.\"",
      "Yorke raises the binoculars. The light resolves: small, white, steady. It is not on the water. It is above it. It is at the height a lamp would be if the lamp were on a mast, except there is no mast, there is nothing, there is only the dark and the water and the light that should not be there.",
      "Emiko and Kael come over the side. Kael sees her face and follows her eyes and goes very still.",
      "\"Is it one of ours?\" Emiko asks.",
      "\"No,\" Yorke says. \"Ours are all behind us.\"",
