      "The second city is called the Lantern.",
      "They learn this at the boom, where a rope is thrown—the rope they brought, two hundred metres of it, thrown back across the last hundred metres of dark so that the Lantern can pull them in—and a woman with a voice like a lighthouse-keeper, which is exactly what she is, hauls them alongside and looks down at five boats of sun-starved faces and says, \"Welcome to the Lantern. You took your time.\"",
