      "Yorke stops walking. \"The array is holding a hole open.\"",
      "\"A hole in the Shade. Small. It drifts—that's why your patch drifted. The hole wanders, and where the hole goes, the light goes, and where the light goes, the fish go, and where the fish go—\" Osei looks at Taryn, who has gone very still, \"—the people follow. You've been measuring the hole, haven't you. You've been putting posts in the water and watching the edge of it move, and you thought the light was dying.\"",
      "\"It was dimming,\" Yorke whispers. \"Eleven percent at the edge.\"",
      "\"The hole is wandering farther from you,\" Osei says. \"Not dying. *Leaving*. We hold it here, over the Lantern, but the mechanism that holds it is old and it drifts, and every year the hole we hold pulls a little farther from the patch it used to warm. Your patch was never yours, child. It was the overflow. The edge of our door. And the door has been moving away from you for two years, and now it's too far to warm you, and you've been standing in the doorway of a house that's being carried away, watching the light go, and thinking the light was going out.\"",
