      "She took them out of the safe. All of them. The physical keys, the hardware tokens, the whole chain of custody of the lid.",
      "And then she did the thing no one had asked her to do, the thing that was not in the plan, the thing she had come all this way to do without telling anyone, because if she had told anyone they would have called it a waste.",
      "She threw them away.",
      "Out the bus's outer hatch, on a vector that would take them into the upper atmosphere, where they would burn, a small bright streak over the Pacific, unnoticed by anyone, unremarked by history, the keys to the lid going home the way everything goes home in the end: as light, briefly, and then as nothing.",
      "\"Burn,\" Riko said.",
      "Then she sealed the hatch, and she strapped into the bus, and she watched the array begin to open — seventy hours of opening, a flower of two hundred and forty facets unfolding over the whole world — and she was alone in the dark at the top of the sky, and the dark was full of light coming the other way, and she was not afraid.",
      "At Baikonur, in the extraction capsule, Garrett Voss watched his own laptop show him the telemetry of the array opening on a sequence he did not command, with keys he did not hold, seventy hours to a dark he could not aim.",
      "He sat very still for a long time.",
      "Then he opened the channel to the pad road, to the woman who had kept his road open both ways, and he said the only true thing he had left.",
      "\"I'm sorry,\" Garrett said.",
      "And the dark came down on everyone, the same."
